Privacy Policy for Medication Wizard
Last updated: May 27, 2026
Wise Owl Studio ("we," "our," or "us") operates the Medication Wizard mobile application (the "Service"). This page informs you of our policies regarding the collection, use, and disclosure of personal data when you use our Service.
1. Information Collection and Use
We do not collect any personally identifiable information (PII) directly through the application. All medication data and history are stored locally on your device or in your private Google Drive (if the Cloud Backup feature is enabled by you).
2. Service Providers
We may employ third-party companies and individuals to facilitate our Service ("Service Providers"), to provide the Service on our behalf, or to perform Service-related services. These third parties have access to your Personal Data only to perform these tasks on our behalf and are obligated not to disclose or use it for any other purpose.
•
Google Play Services: Used for app functionality and account management.
•
AdMob: Used to display advertisements. AdMob may collect certain data for personalized advertising.
•
Firebase Analytics & Crashlytics: Used to monitor app usage and technical stability to help us improve the experience.
•
Google Play Billing: Used to process premium upgrades securely. We do not see or store your credit card information.
3. Data Storage (Room Database & SharedPreferences)
Your health data is stored using Android's Room Persistence Library and SharedPreferences on your own device. This data remains on your phone unless you choose to create a manual backup or use the Premium Cloud Backup feature to your own Google Drive account.
4. Children's Privacy
Our Service does not address anyone under the age of 13. We do not knowingly collect personally identifiable information from children under 13.
5. Changes to This Privacy Policy
We may update our Privacy Policy from time to time. We will notify you of any changes by posting the new Privacy Policy on this page.
